No OpenStreetMap data is bundled or redistributed. A deployment operator (or a
user, per visit) may configure an external raster tile source, typically
OSM-derived; those tiles are requested by the user's browser directly from the
configured provider and are credited on the map, as ODbL section 4.3 requires
of publicly used Produced Works. See docs/HOSTING.md.

Runtime and development dependencies retain their own licences, as declared in
backend/pyproject.toml and frontend/package.json.

